            "sha256": "6fc7de23121f5950f5f9d8a7852fc65fbc3fcd01ba5db71c1ca4f1ab839c72f4",
            "size_bytes": 32492372,
            "signature": "",
            "changelog_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/shemondotme/oeparts/main/CHANGELOG.md",
            "download_url": "https://github.com/shemondotme/oeparts/releases/download/v2.0.3/oeparts-2.0.3.zip",
            "git_commit_sha": "dee783589ab598222372e07ca25597374a3e6bff",
            "git_signature": "",
            "pre_update_notes": "A small patch on top of 2.0.2: the device-alert service worker now lives at /admin/service-worker instead of /admin/sw.js, because nginx setups such as CloudPanel answer every .js address from disk and never reach the app. No database changes. If the phone icon in your top bar did nothing on 2.0.2, this is the fix. The static files in public/admin-push/ must be readable by your web server (chmod -R go+rX public/admin-push) \u2014 on some hosts a freshly created folder is not."
        },
        {
            "version": "2.0.2",
            "codename": "Lifeline",
            "release_date": "2026-10-06",
            "channel": "stable",
            "security": false,
            "min_php": "8.3",
            "min_mysql": "8.0.16",
            "min_version_to_update_from": "2.0.0",
            "migration_count": 2,
            "sha256": "583ed75a78e69fb56f3a7eee5426dd342dac2a1a6a361fd3fa442e203206ae7b",
            "size_bytes": 32491209,
            "signature": "",
            "changelog_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/shemondotme/oeparts/main/CHANGELOG.md",
            "download_url": "https://github.com/shemondotme/oeparts/releases/download/v2.0.2/oeparts-2.0.2.zip",
            "git_commit_sha": "c560459a35661199c7659fd8fe9501c67275b0c6",
            "git_signature": "",
            "pre_update_notes": "Update straight from 2.0.0. 2.0.1 was published but its update got stuck at the first (\"backup\") step on large catalogs, and everything it contained ships here. That stall is fixed in this release: the pre-update backup now runs a few chunks per request instead of one request that could outlast your host's time limit \u2014 but the fix lives in the NEW code, so an install still running 2.0.0 must be updated by hand once (see the manual update steps in the release notes); later updates should be able to use the in-app updater again. The update applies 2 small, additive database migrations (an admin permission and the tables behind the new device alerts), none of which touch your product, order or customer tables. If this is a git-managed install, take a database backup first and pick a quiet hour; the site is in maintenance mode briefly while it runs."
        },
        {
            "version": "2.0.1",
            "codename": "Failsafe",
            "release_date": "2026-10-05",
            "channel": "stable",
            "security": false,
            "min_php": "8.3",
            "min_mysql": "8.0.16",
            "min_version_to_update_from": "2.0.0",
            "migration_count": 1,
            "sha256": "3c777186ba6621e2908c6a341557481f4dec1ec40bd2a3ed68958afc93b59c1a",
            "size_bytes": 31648509,
            "signature": "",
            "changelog_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/shemondotme/oeparts/main/CHANGELOG.md",
            "download_url": "https://github.com/shemondotme/oeparts/releases/download/v2.0.1/oeparts-2.0.1.zip",
            "git_commit_sha": "13ea7b705de56744fafe78d8262ca3d51fc6a08e",
            "git_signature": "",
            "pre_update_notes": "This release fixes a real incident: a git-managed install whose update was interrupted during the git checkout step (for example, a slow network pull hitting your host's own request timeout) was not rolled back automatically, leaving the site on broken code with an un-migrated database until an admin fixed it by hand. That is now handled automatically, both by the update engine itself and by the hourly watchdog. It also adds a System \u2192 Cleanup admin page (safely removes any dev-only files an interrupted update left behind, plus a read-only database health check \u2014 it only ever reports, never deletes), and a redesigned OE Recovery console (the framework-free emergency fallback used when the app can't boot at all) with a real application-log viewer, environment/preflight checks, and copy-paste recovery commands. One new, safe migration. README.md, SECURITY.md and CHANGELOG.md no longer ship on installed sites."
        },
        {
            "version": "2.0.0",
            "codename": "Bulletproof",
            "release_date": "2026-09-25",
            "channel": "stable",
            "security": false,
            "min_php": "8.3",
            "min_mysql": "8.0.16",
            "min_version_to_update_from": "1.0.16",
            "migration_count": 21,
            "sha256": "fb33b6425db5452a91d58a634370c3c863488550bf9eccd18324ae447b4ef25f",
            "size_bytes": 31641026,
            "signature": "",
            "changelog_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/shemondotme/oeparts/main/CHANGELOG.md",
            "download_url": "https://github.com/shemondotme/oeparts/releases/download/v2.0.0/oeparts-2.0.0.zip",
            "git_commit_sha": "2bc26c1d2e9fa6706140a5d664dd86a9e9a364e0",
            "git_signature": "",
            "breaking_changes": [
                "Paysera: the separate 'Webhook Signoff Secret' setting is gone. Paysera signs its callbacks with your Client Secret, which is now what is verified. Re-check the Paysera fields in your payment settings after updating.",
                "Airwallex: webhooks are now verified and interpreted exactly as Airwallex documents them (the previous signature, timestamp and event-name handling could not have matched a real Airwallex webhook). Make sure the webhook URL is registered in your Airwallex dashboard and its signing secret is saved in your payment settings.",
                "Checkout progress is now held in the cache rather than the session, so customers who are part-way through checkout when the update finishes will be asked to restart checkout from their (preserved) cart."
            ],
            "pre_update_notes": "Update straight from 1.0.16 \u2014 1.0.17, 1.0.18 and 1.0.19 were never published as installable releases, and everything from them ships in 2.0.0. The update takes a backup first and applies 21 database migrations, all of which are safe to re-run. On a catalog of around a million products, adding the new columns rebuilds the products table once, which takes several minutes while the site is in maintenance mode \u2014 pick a quiet hour. Both payment gateways were rewritten to match Airwallex's and Paysera's own documentation in this release; they are covered by automated tests but have not yet been run against the vendors' live sandboxes, so make a test payment before relying on either in production. Once the progress bar reaches \u201cRunning migrations\u201d your open page may stop updating by itself \u2014 that is expected: the update keeps running on the server and finishes on its own, so leave it alone and reload System Updates after a few minutes to see the result."
        },
